codex
The candidate’s ground entry cases and a concrete loop-precondition witness both close with `#Top`, and their outputs agree with both Python implementations for the positive-domain cases. The literal-module check confirms the early-return branch but also shows why the universal loop bridge cannot apply to a normally loaded module: its proved summary requires module scope 0 to be exactly empty, while `FuncDef` leaves the `x_or_y` binding there. I’m keeping this real-program-pinning limitation separate from the candidate’s successful direct-closure theorem while I run the mandatory false-result test.
